-- EXPECT-ERROR: Unknown type `NoSuchType` in `derive`
-- Finding 17: `derive X for UnknownType` must ERROR, not silently no-op.
-- `expand_derive` (`desugar.ml`) previously returned a bare `[]` when the
-- derive TARGET TYPE was not found in the module's `type_defs`, emitting no
-- diagnostic — so `derive Show for NoSuchType` typechecked clean (exit 0),
-- making a misspelled type name indistinguishable from a no-op. The `None`
-- branch now mirrors its sibling (unknown derive INTERFACE) and emits an
-- `Err.error` before returning `[]`. See core-march-types.md §2.4.
mod Main do
  derive Show for NoSuchType

  fn main() : Int do 0 end
end
